{
  "ideas": [
    {
      "id": 3,
      "name": "Goo Rides",
      "approach": "handmade",
      "approachWhy": "Each ride is a small timed puzzle (where it goes, when it stops, when to get off), and the timings have to be tuned by hand so boarding and leaving windows stay fair. A random generator would make many rides that look the same or have impossible handoffs.",
      "engine": {
        "have": [
          "slide motion on x, y or z (sin path, phase per part) that already carries a player standing on it",
          "phase offsets so several rides run out of step (LilyLift, BobbingDiscs)",
          "a stand-on trigger for the local player (melt) to copy for sinking rides",
          "red see-through hazard goo that sends you back to the start",
          "step gap and rise tests (GAP_MAX 6, RISE_MAX 3.5) for the parts at rest",
          "red goo touch = back to the start pad (shared hazard reset that ideas 1, 8, 14 and 25 also list)"
        ],
        "new": [
          {
            "what": "'shuttle' slide (same name and code as idea 25 Sliding Maze): hold at a stop, move, hold at the next stop, instead of a pure sin wave; rides add an optional list of stops so one ride can visit 3 stops in turn (Wrong Stop)",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "rail line under each ride and a dotted ghost of its next stop (the 'you can tell by' look); the ghost also shows which stop comes next on a multi-stop ride",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "'sink' motion (same one ideas 2 Melting Floor and 12 Rising Goo plan): lowers while the local player stands on it, rises back once left; here it runs on top of a moving ride",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "waits-for-you trigger: ride sits at its dock until you step on, runs once, comes back empty (client only); same one-shot stand-on start as idea 21's one-shot geyser and idea 24's collapse clock, so build it once",
            "size": "M"
          },
          {
            "what": "carry on moving parts: share idea 4's fix (client reads the moving part's live position) so walking across a moving deck and jumping off a moving ride keep you with it; check in Studio that air control does not brake you",
            "size": "S"
          },
          {
            "what": "test support: check the closest gap between a moving ride and its dock or the next ride, not only at rest (idea 15's swing reach check and idea 4's moving-pad check can share this helper)",
            "size": "M"
          }
        ]
      },
      "readability": "Every ride is a wide jelly raft with a rail line under it and a dotted ghost of where it stops next, plus a soft hum that rises as it speeds up. A ride that sinks bubbles and gurgles, and red see-through goo sits where a ride you must leave is heading.",
